! ax4b_5gh_prog_ix_v_minus.strap -- jb_ax4b "I-BOX 4", routine 148 (1248, "INDEX
! MODIFICATION TEST", banner PDF p.113: "TEST5. CHECK PROGRESSIVE
! INDEXING, EIGHT CODES."), TESTs 5G and 5H, "CHK PROG IX V-IC" and
! "CHK PROG IX V-ICR":
!
!   PDF p.151  011242.00-011267.40  both tests, exit, continuity
!   PDF p.153  011352.00-011371.00  148K25-148K28, 148XW4-148XW9
!   PDF p.191  013075.00            BIT17
!
! Routine 148's other progressive pair, TESTs 5E/5F (V+ICR, V-I), is
! ibox4_prog_ix_v.strap.  No printed page numbers on these sheets: cited
! by PDF page and octal location.  Read from the page images at 150 dpi;
! checked row for row by tests/verify_ax4b_5gh_prog_ix_v_minus_listing.py
! (53 rows, 6 symbols).
!
! WHAT IT TESTS (IBM's code, unchanged).  Each test loads X1 from a
! control word (I48XW8 (148K27, count 2); I48XW9 (148K27, count 1, refill 148K28)), does ONE progressive VFL load
! "L(code)(BU,64,8),1.0($X1)", and asks four questions, each with its
! own SIC,SEN / BZXE,SERS:
!   KV $X2 vs 148K25   the operand (148K25 = 148K27 = 123456.70) arrived
!                      ($X2 loaded from $R);
!   KV $X1 vs 148K28   the index value: value - 1.0 = 011353 (V-IC: count 2 -> 1, no refill); V-ICR:
!   count 1 -> 0, so X1 is REFILLED from 148K28 (value 011353, count 1);
!   KC $X1 vs BIT17    the count, against bits 0-17 of BIT17's first
!                      half-word, i.e. its value 1.00 (Reference Manual
!                      printed p.24, PDF 27, Compare Count, read in the
!                      page image): count 1 is expected after both codes;
!   SR,$X1,$X1 / LX,$X1,$X1 / BZXVZ   SR puts X1's refill in bits 0-17
!                      of the half-word at word 17 -- X1's own value
!                      field -- and zeroes bits 18-24 (p.24, Store
!                      Refill), so the value must read zero: "REFILLED"
!                      otherwise.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS (not on these pages):
!   * SSIP's entry points: SSW (001301.00) is a PASS halt, SERS
!     (001304.00) a FAIL halt, SEN/SENO (001310.00/001311.00) data words
!     SIC stores into.  The addresses are the listing's own (B,SSW
!     prints "1301.10 00", SIC,SEN "1310.00 80", BZXE,SERS "1304.32 C0",
!     SIC,SENO+.32 "1311.40 80"); the contents are SSIP's, which is not
!     transcribed.  SIC "is executed if and only if the associated
!     branching is successful" (Reference Manual printed p.41, PDF 44),
!     so SEN stays 0 on a pass and names the failing check otherwise.
!   * Notation only: "%" and the box glyph are "(" and ")"; the label
!     glyph the scan shows as "1" is the letter I (I48..), as for every
!     ax4b label (docs/listing_typography.md).  Nothing else changed.
!   * IC248 and BIT2 are SYN'd from the printed "LX,$X13,IC248"
!     (11306.32 10) and "V+,$X12,BIT2"; the continuity rows after B,SSW
!     are never run.
!
! RESULT ON THE MODEL, 2026-11-18 (a57832f + this deck): PASSES -- halts
! at SSW (PC 1410), SEN = 0, X1 = 0x40000 (value 0 after the SR, count
! 1, refill 0), X2 = 148K25's word (0x29CBB80000000000).  CYCLES 500
! is MODEL BEHAVIOUR; no time is printed.  IBM's listing and the model
! AGREE.
!
! INJECTIONS, each in a scratch copy of bsv/, OBSERVED for this deck:
!   count decremented only for codes ending 3 (V-IC no longer counts) ->
!     FAIL halt, SEN 011250.40: TEST 5G's KC check, CYCLES 201.
!   refill suppressed -> FAIL halt, SEN 011261.00: TEST 5H's KC check (count
!     left 0, not refilled to 1), CYCLES 408.
!   CONTROL: the unmodified model, the pins below (PASS, SEN = 0).
!   Each built in a scratch copy of bsv/ and restored (cmp IDENTICAL).
!
! ---- SSIP's entry points: SUBSTITUTES (not on these pages) -----------
! The addresses are the ones this listing prints for them (SIC,SEN
! "1310.00 80", B,SERS "1304.10 00", SIC,SENO+.32 "1311.40 80", B,SSW
! "1301.10 00"), the same as routine 148's; what is AT them is SSIP's,
! which this file replaces with halts, as ax4b_148_immediate_indexed does.
        SLC, (8)1301.0
SSW     BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: PASS (the return to SSIP)
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: FAIL (SSIP's error report)
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's error link word
SENO    DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's other link word
!
! IC248 and BIT2: SYN from the printed addresses of "LX,$X13,IC248"
! (11306.32 10) and "V+,$X12,BIT2" (13056.30 B0); the continuity
! rows after B,SSW are never run (SSW halts first).
IC248   SYN, (8)11306.0
BIT2    SYN, (8)13056.0
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.151, 011242.00-011267.40 (no printed page number on the sheet)
! ======================================================================
        SLC, (8)11242.00
I4847   LX,  $X1, I48XW8               ! -TEST 5G, CHK PROG IX V-IC.
        L(V-IC)(BU,64,8), 1.0($X1)
        LX,  $X2, $R
        KV,  $X2, I48K25
        SIC, SEN                      ! -VFL LOAD PROG INDEXED, CODE V-IC,
        BZXE, SERS                    ! -FAILED TO OBTAIN CORRECT OPERAND.
!
        KV,  $X1, I48K28
        SIC, SEN                      ! -VFL LOAD PROG INDEXED, CODE V-IC,
        BZXE, SERS                    ! -FAILED TO MODIFY IX VALUE CORRECTLY.
!
        KC,  $X1, BIT17
        SIC, SEN                      ! -VFL LOAD PROG INDEXED, CODE V-IC,
        BZXE, SERS                    ! -MODIFIED INDEX COUNT INCORRECTLY.
!
        SR,  $X1, $X1
        LX,  $X1, $X1
        SIC, SEN                      ! -VFL LOAD PROG INDEXED, CODE V-IC,
        BZXVZ, SERS                   ! -REFILLED.
!
        LX,  $X1, I48XW9               ! -TEST 5H, CHK PROG IX V-ICR.
        L(V-ICR)(BU,64,8), 1.0($X1)
        LX,  $X2, $R
        KV,  $X2, I48K25
        SIC, SEN                      ! -VFL LOAD PROG INDEXED, CODE V-ICR,
        BZXE, SERS                    ! -FAILED TO OBTAIN CORRECT OPERAND.
!
        KV,  $X1, I48K28
        SIC, SEN                      ! -VFL LOAD PROG INDEXED, CODE V-ICR,
        BZXE, SERS                    ! -FAILED TO MODIFY IX VALUE CORRECTLY.
!
        KC,  $X1, BIT17
        SIC, SEN                      ! -VFL LOAD PROG INDEXED, CODE V-ICR,
        BZXE, SERS                    ! -MODIFIED INDEX COUNT INCORRECTLY.
!
        SR,  $X1, $X1
        LX,  $X1, $X1
        SIC, SEN                      ! -VFL LOAD PROG INDEXED, CODE V-ICR,
        BZXVZ, SERS                   ! -REFILLED INCORRECTLY.
!
        B,   $+1.0
        BD,  I4847
        SIC, SENO+.32
        B,   SSW                      ! -TO SSIP
        BD,  $+.32
!
        LX,  $X13, IC248              ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY.
        SC,  $X13, $X12
        V+,  $X12, BIT2
        LC,  $X13, $X12
        SX,  $X13, IC248
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.153, 011352.00-011371.00: routine 148's constants
! ======================================================================
        SLC, (8)11352.0
I48K25  XW,  (8)123456.70
I48K26  XW,  (8)765432.10
I48K27  XW,  (8)123456.70
I48K28  XW,  I48K26, 1, 0
        SLC, (8)11364.0
I48XW4  XW,  I48K25, 1, 0
I48XW5  XW,  I48K25, 2, 0
I48XW6  XW,  I48K25, 1, I48K28
I48XW7  XW,  I48K27, 1, 0
I48XW8  XW,  I48K27, 2, 0
I48XW9  XW,  I48K27, 1, I48K28
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.191, 013075.00: BIT17 (value 1.00), the count KC compares with
! ======================================================================
        SLC, (8)13075.0
BIT17   XW,  (8)1.00, 0, 0
        END, I4847
